# Auto-detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# ⛔ CONTENT-ADDRESSED BLOBS ARE NEVER NORMALISED. THE FILE'S NAME IS THE HASH OF ITS BYTES.
#
# `* text=auto` above asks git to GUESS whether a file is text, and for a blob under
# `blobs/sha256/<hex>` it guesses wrong in the one way that matters: an OCI manifest or config blob
# is JSON, carries no NUL, and is therefore treated as text and line-ending-converted on checkout.
# 476 bytes become 491, the content no longer hashes to the name it is stored under, and
# `mantle.oci.layout` refuses it — correctly, because verifying content against its ref is the whole
# contract of the store.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS INVISIBLE ON THE MACHINE THAT COMMITTED IT AND FATAL EVERYWHERE ELSE. The blobs in the
# git objects are byte-correct (measured 2026-08-23: all three hash to their own names). The damage
# happens at CHECKOUT, so the working tree that captured the fixture keeps passing forever while
# every FRESH CLONE fails — which is precisely every CI runner. It was found by the first sovereign
# cycle in 25 days: five green tests here, five red in `_ci-work`, same commit.
#
# `-text` disables all conversion in both directions; `-diff` stops git rendering the bytes as text
# in a diff. Applied to the tree rather than to one file, because the next captured layout will have
# different names by construction — the names ARE hashes, so an allowlist of them cannot be written
# in advance.
tests/fixtures/oci-layout-real/blobs/** -text -diff

# Force LF for shell scripts (critical for Docker containers)
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Force LF for Python files
*.py text eol=lf

# Force LF for Docker-related files
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf

# Force LF for config files
*.conf text eol=lf
*.config text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
*.caddy text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Windows-specific files can keep CRLF
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
